SUMMARY:Beyond Cornell: What the Research Tells Us About Sex Education\, Consent\, and Safer Communities
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Eva Goldfarb\, Professor of Public Health at Montclair State University\, for a compelling\, evidence-based discussion on why comprehensive sex education is essential for building healthier\, safer communities. Dr. Goldfarb is the lead author of a landmark study demonstrating that comprehensive sex education does far more than reduce unintended pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections. It strengthens communication skills\, healthy relationships\, and reduces sexual violence. Dr. Goldfarb will discuss these findings as well as her recent research on sexual consent\, offering important insights into why what we teach in our schools (and at home) matters long before students reach college. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/beyond-cornell-what-the-research-tells-us-about-sex-education-consent-and-safer-communities/
